# Environment Variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
In production, prefer setting these as system environment variables rather than using a `.env` file.

# ─── Required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Session signing secret — REQUIRED in production.
# Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
MSPC_SECRET=

# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# HTTP port (default: 3000)
# MSPC_PORT=3000

# Data directory for config, agent workspaces, logs (default: ~/.mspc)
# MSPC_DATA_DIR=/home/youruser/.mspc

# Public URL, used for WebSocket upgrades and cookie domain in production
# MSPC_PUBLIC_URL=https://office.example.com

# Node.js environment — set to 'production' in production deployments
# NODE_ENV=production
